#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:132
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Mutter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:135
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Fix an issue with the tests that would otherwise require the package to be "
"built with debugging information:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:139
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">sed \"/tests_c_args =/s/$/ + ['-U', 'G_DISABLE_ASSERT']/\" -i src/tests/meson.build &amp;&amp;\n"
"sed \"/c_args:/a '-U', 'G_DISABLE_ASSERT',\" -i src/tests/cogl/unit/meson.build</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:143
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Mutter</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:147
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup --prefix=/usr            \\\n"
"            --buildtype=release      \\\n"
"            -D tests=disabled        \\\n"
"            -D profiler=false        \\\n"
"            -D bash_completion=false \\\n"
"            ..                       &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:159
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you want to run the test suite, ensure <xref linkend='python-dbusmock'/> "
"is installed and issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:163
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>meson configure -D tests=enabled &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja test</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:167
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The tests require an active Wayland session. Some tests are flaky "
"(especially if your system is under a high load), so if a test fails you can"
" try to run a specific test again by using the <command>meson test "
"<replaceable>&lt;test name&gt;</replaceable></command> command.  A few tests"
" may fail depending on some system configuration.  Don't make any mouse or "
"keyboard input while the test suite is running or some tests may fail.  You "
"can also test basic functions of <application>Mutter</application> following"
" <xref linkend='mutter-starting' role=','/> after installing this package."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:181
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:184
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:189
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:195
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D bash_completion=false</parameter>: Allows building this "
"package without the <ulink url=\"https://github.com/scop/bash-"
"completion/\">bash-completion</ulink> package installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:202
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D tests=disabled</parameter>: Allows building this package "
"without <xref linkend='python-dbusmock'/> installed.  It'll be overridden "
"with <command>meson configure</command> if running the test suite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:209
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D profiler=false</parameter>: Allows building this package "
"without <application>Sysprof</application>.  Remove this option if you've "
"installed <application>Sysprof</application> and want to analyze the "
"rendering performance of <application>Mutter</application>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:216
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>-D x11=true</option>: Allows building this package with X11 support."
" X11 support is deprecated and will be removed in GNOME 50."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:223
#, xml-text
msgid "Starting Mutter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:232
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Mutter</application> is normally used as a component of "
"<application>gnome-shell</application>, but it can be used as a standalone "
"Wayland compositor too.  To run <application>Mutter</application> as a "
"Wayland compositor, in a virtual console, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:239
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>mutter --wayland -- vte-2.91</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:242
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Replace <command>vte-2.91</command> with the command line for the first "
"application you want in the Wayland session. Note that once this application"
" exits, the Wayland session will be terminated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:248
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Mutter</application> can also function as a nested compositor "
"in another Wayland session.  In a terminal emulator, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:252
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>MUTTER_DEBUG_DUMMY_MODE_SPECS=1920x1080 mutter --wayland --nested"
" -- vte-2.91</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/gnome/platform/mutter.xml:255
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Replace <replaceable>1920x1080</replaceable> with the size you want for the "
"nested Wayland session."
msgstr ""

